.TH RAYGAMES 1
.SH NAME
arkanoid, asteroids, missile, raygames \- three raylib arcade games
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B games/arkanoid
[
.B -n
.I frames
] [
.B -s
.I seed
] [
.B -o
.I image.png
]
.br
.B games/asteroids
[
.I options
]
.br
.B games/missile
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These games run in rio windows using the native raylib and TinyGL libraries.
They need no external game data.
.PP
.I Arkanoid
breaks bricks with a bouncing ball.
Left and Right move the paddle; Space launches the ball.
.PP
.I Asteroids
flies a ship among rocks that split when shot.
Left and Right turn, Up accelerates, Down brakes, and Space fires.
.PP
.I Missile
runs Missile Commander: protect cities and launchers from incoming missiles.
Aim with the mouse; buttons 1, 2 and 3 fire from the left, middle and right
launchers respectively.
.PP
In all three games, P pauses, R restarts and Escape exits.
Enter starts a new round after losing.
Resizing preserves the arena's aspect ratio and adjusts mouse aiming.
.PP
.B -n
exits after the given number of displayed frames.
.B -s
sets the random seed for a repeatable game.
.B -o
saves the last displayed frame as a PNG image before exiting.
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/games/raygames
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR games (1),
.IR raylib (2),
.IR tinygl (2),
.IR gpu (3)
.SH BUGS
Requires a VirtIO GPU with VirGL and its host-owner access.
The original frame-based game logic is paced at 60 frames per second;
slower rendering slows play.
These single-round games have no audio or saved scores.
